      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T18:15:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Scott: I follow the VIF logic, but I can\u0027t remember what prompted you to set `Type_C_Can_Act_As_Device` to true in the first place. Can you remind me?",
      "parentUuid": "39c02abd_22813558",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65dcd78a_cc9a043f",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-26T15:14:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wouldn\u0027t we expect the muxes to be in TBT mode before mode exit? \n\nI assume we want to NAK if we hadn\u0027t actually been in TBT mode before the ExitMode came, and ACK if we were in TBT mode.  Though obviously if the compliance tests say otherwise, we can also ACK when we weren\u0027t previously in the mode.",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e575a54_fd5896b3",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329118
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T00:55:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My original thought was follow SPEC said that we should in USB operation or the USB Safe State. But I think check mux to be in TBT mode before exit will make more sense because we will enter TBT mode before exit it.\n\nShould we just check `USB_PD_MUX_TBT_COMPAT_ENABLED` or also check `USB_PD_MUX_USB_ENABLED` and `USB_PD_MUX_SAFE_MODE`?",
      "parentUuid": "65dcd78a_cc9a043f",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e139cff_1b396822",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T18:15:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From PD rev 1.3, v 1.4, ss 6.4.4.3.5 Exit Mode Command (I know v 1.5 was published):\n\u003e The Responder Shall ... only return a NAK acknowledgement to a request not containing an Active Mode (i.e., Invalid object position).\n\nI take that to mean that the TCPM should NAK an Exit Mode if we haven\u0027t previously entered a mode. (The language seems to allow for an ACK, but it would be a no-op.) The canonical way to check active modes in our codebase is `pd_get_partner_active_modes`. If the returned structure doesn\u0027t contain the SVID from the _Exit Mode_`, the TCPM should NAK.",
      "parentUuid": "2e575a54_fd5896b3",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
